<section class="home-section">
  <h2>Built as I learned it</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>After learning the basics of high school calculus, I got fixated on complex functions. The idea that there was a whole field of math on numbers that aren't even <em>Real</em> fascinated me. After many hours of staring at complex-analysis.com, I knew I didn't have the tools to explore the subject yet, but I would definitely be back. Finishing Multivariable and learning enough vector calculus by the end of my senior year finally let me tackle this topic: what analysis on complex functions actually looks like.</p>
    <p>I'm Max, an incoming math major at UCSB's College of Creative Studies. This site isn't a textbook; much better ones already exist. It's a record of the path I carved through the subject: the lessons I wanted to learn, as I actually learned them, bumps included.</p>
    <p>The system behind it (session structure, spaced review, a running profile of how I learn, and the actual prompts that commissioned each visualization) is written up in <a href="/how-i-built-this/">How I built this</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

